      "role": "user",
      "content": "<|channel>thought\n<channel|>That's a bit wordy for a podcast bit. It reads more like an essay about a joke than the actual joke itself. I need the actual lines for the script, not a description of the concept. \n\nCan you just write out the actual dialogue? Make it punchy. Focus on the part where the characters are actually making fun of the \"always surrounded by family\" thing or the \"constant food smells.\" Give me the actual script lines that characters would say to each other.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
